.TH PBOX 1 "2026-11" "PHPBox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pbox, phpbox \- manage PHP Docker projects and shared PHP environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pbox
.RI [ options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.br
.B pbox help
.RI [ command " [subcommand]]"
.br
.B pbox help --all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a command, open the graphical application. CLI commands work without a graphical session.
Project data is stored under ~/php-dev/projects; shared environments are under ~/php-dev/environments.
Use --help for examples, or help --all for the complete command reference in Chinese.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -p ", " --project " NAME"
Select a project explicitly. Otherwise detect the project from the current directory.
.TP
.BR -C ", " --directory " DIR"
Change the host working directory before running the command.
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quiet
Suppress PHPBox progress, not errors or child program output. list prints names only; env list prints IDs only.
.TP
.BR -T ", " --no-tty
Disable the pseudo-terminal. Suitable for pipelines and redirection.
.TP
.BR -t ", " --tty
Force a pseudo-terminal. By default both stdin and stdout must be terminals.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show full underlying operation errors.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all projects. Supports --json and -q.
.TP
.BR status ", " ps " [NAME]"
Show the selected project, or all projects outside a project directory. --all forces all projects.
--check fails unless every selected project is healthy. Supports --json.
.TP
.BR start ", " up " [NAME]"
Start project services and the shared PHP environment if needed.
.TP
.B stop [NAME]
Stop project services; retain containers and the shared PHP environment.
.TP
.B restart [NAME]
Restart existing project containers. Does not apply new images or recreate shared PHP.
.TP
.B recreate [NAME]
Recreate project containers from existing images/configuration; retain named volumes, replace container writable layers.
.TP
.B down [NAME]
Remove project containers, retain project files and named volumes. Shared PHP remains running.
.TP
.BR build ", " rebuild " [NAME] [--no-cache]"
Build independent project images only; these are aliases. Run recreate to apply new images.
.TP
.B logs [NAME]
Print the last 200 lines and exit. -f follows; --tail N|all, --since TIME,
--timestamps, --no-color and --service php|nginx|mysql|redis|cron are supported.
Shared environment logs may contain output from other projects.
.TP
.B shell [OPTIONS] [SERVICE]
Open a container shell; default service is php. Supports -u USER, -w WORKDIR, -T and -t.
.TP
.B exec [OPTIONS] SERVICE [--] COMMAND [ARGS...]
Execute a command verbatim. PHPBox options must precede SERVICE.
.TP
.BR php ", " composer ", " artisan ", " think " [ARGS...]"
Forward arguments verbatim, including --help. Put PHPBox options before the command.
Use pbox help php (etc.) for wrapper help. A leading -- separator is removed.
PHP and Composer preserve the current code subdirectory; framework commands use the code root.
.TP
.B env ACTION
Actions: list, inspect, create, start, stop, restart, rebuild, delete.
Select environments by full ID or unique name. list/inspect support --json.
create NAME --php VERSION accepts repeated --extension EXT, --proxy URL and --start.
It builds but does not start by default; failed builds retain files for retry.
rebuild accepts --no-cache and updates running environments.
Stopping, restarting or rebuilding bound environments requires confirmation (-y/--yes for scripts).
delete always requires confirmation and refuses bound environments.
.TP
.B use ENV [--check] [--json]
Switch the selected project to a PHP environment. Supports upgrades and downgrades,
without enforcing Composer requirements or importing the old php.ini.
--check validates without switching; it may start the target environment and generate project identity.
.TP
.B recover [NAME]
Restore an incomplete project environment switch using its recovery record.
.TP
.B doctor [--json]
Check Docker, Compose and daemon connectivity. Missing required components fail the command.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print a completion script; source it or install it in the shell completion directory.
.TP
.B gui [--hide|--new-project]
Open the GUI, optionally hidden or with the new-project dialog.
.SH OUTPUT AND EXIT STATUS
Results use stdout; PHPBox progress and errors use stderr. JSON uses stable English field names.
0 means success, 1 operational failure, 2 invalid arguments, 130 interrupt, 143 SIGTERM,
141 closed output pipe. Container command exit statuses are preserved.
Stopped projects do not fail status unless --check is used; Docker query failures always fail.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pbox -p workbench php -r 'echo PHP_VERSION;'
pbox -C ~/php-dev/projects/demo composer install
pbox exec -T mysql -- mysql --defaults-extra-file=/tmp/client.cnf < backup.sql
pbox logs -f --service php --since 1h
pbox env create php84 --php 8.4 --extension redis --start
pbox -p workbench use php84 --check
pbox env restart php84 --yes
pbox list --json
pbox help --all
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
docker(1), php(1)
